<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $75.9 mln Feb 5.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $75.9 mln Feb 5.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $75.9 million surplus on Feb 5 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 5</p>
<p>Exports: $182.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $152.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $304.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $258.6 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $75.9 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $591.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $408.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $642.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $560.9 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $264.3 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>(-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418)</p>
</text>
